| Situation             | Use  |
| --------------------- | ---- |
| Normal program output | cout |
| Debug messages        | cerr |
| Logging errors        | cerr |
| Progress updates      | cout |


cerr usage
	Buffered output may not appear before crash.
	Use cerr for crash diagnostics.
	In embedded systems, buffering behavior matters.

Difference between cout and cerr?
	cout is buffered and used for normal output, while cerr is unbuffered and used for error output.
	cerr flushes immediately, making it suitable for debugging.
	Both can be redirected separately since they map to stdout and stderr.